# C++ if-else

## Description

This program demonstrates the use of the `if-else` selection statement in C++. It checks whether a student has passed or failed based on the marks obtained.

## Variables Used

### 1. marks
Stores the student's marks.

## Main Function

The `main()` function stores the student's marks and checks whether the marks are greater than or equal to 40.

If the condition is true, the program displays `Pass`. Otherwise, it displays `Fail`.

## Output

Pass

## Concept Used

- Selection Statement
- if-else Statement
- Conditional Checking

## Program Flow

Start
  ↓
Store Student Marks
  ↓
Check marks >= 40
  ↓
Yes ─────→ Display "Pass"
  ↓
No ──────→ Display "Fail"
  ↓
End